{
  "id": "pacs.010.001.03",
  "short": "pacs.010",
  "name": "FinancialInstitutionDirectDebit",
  "domain": "pacs",
  "label": "Financial Institution Direct Debit",
  "direction": "bank → bank",
  "mtEquivalent": [
    "MT204"
  ],
  "related": [
    "pacs.009",
    "pacs.003",
    "pacs.002"
  ],
  "summary": "One financial institution debits another's account under a pre-existing authority. The bank-to-bank counterpart of a direct debit, with no customer involved.",
  "whenUsed": "Narrow and specialist: reimbursement claims between institutions, collecting fees or margin from a correspondent, and settlement of obligations where a standing authority already exists. Replaces MT204. Because it pulls funds from another institution's account, access is normally governed by a bilateral agreement rather than open scheme membership.",
  "gotchas": [
    "There is no mandate structure here as there is in pacs.003 — the authority is bilateral and outside the message. Nothing in the message proves you were entitled to debit, so operational controls carry that weight.",
    "The creditor is the one sending the message and receiving the funds, which is the opposite of the pacs.009 convention. Mapping the two messages with shared code needs care.",
    "Many schemes do not support this message at all. Check bilateral and scheme agreements before building a flow around it."
  ],
